In macOS 27 Golden Gate, Siri AI is a lot smarter than before, so it doesn't always flail and attempt to hand your questions over to ChatGPT. However, if you still prefer OpenAI's chatbot for certain queries, you can still ask for it explicitly. <br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/03/macos-27-siri-spotlight.jpg" alt="" width="1960" height="1307" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1057872" /><br/>
In macOS Tahoe, Siri would suggest passing a request to ChatGPT when it thought the chatbot could help. In macOS 27 though, ChatGPT only answers when you specifically ask it. There's also no setting that makes ChatGPT your default assistant – as things stand, you need to choose it for each query. Here's how it's done.<br/>
<br/>
<h2>Turn On the ChatGPT Extension</h2><br/>
<ol><br/>
  <li>Open <strong>System Settings</strong>.</li><br/>
  <li>Click <strong>Siri</strong> in the sidebar.</li><br/>
  <li>Click <strong>ChatGPT</strong> under "Extension."<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/chatgpt-not-siri.jpg" alt="settings" width="1618" height="1194" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1067766" /><br/>
  <li>Turn on <strong>Use Extension</strong>.</li><br/>
  <li>Choose whether to sign in with a ChatGPT account.<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/ask-chatgpt-not-siri-macos-271.jpg" alt="settings" width="1514" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1067754" /></ol><br/>
<br/>
If you sign in, your requests are saved to your ChatGPT chat history (OpenAI's privacy policies apply). If you skip sign-in, OpenAI receives nothing tied to your Apple Account and it can't store your requests.<br/>
<br/>
<h2>Ask ChatGPT in Search or Ask</h2><br/>
<ol><br/>
  <li>Press <strong>Command-Space</strong> to open the <strong>Search or Ask</strong> bar (formerly Spotlight Search).</li><br/>
  <li>Right-click (or Control-click) the field.</li><br/>
  <li>Choose <strong>Ask</strong> ➝ <strong>Use ChatGPT</strong>.</li><br/>
  <li>Type your question, then press Enter.<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/ask-siri-chatgpt.jpg" alt="siri" width="1358" height="272" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1067755" /><br/>
</ol>When an answer comes back, unless there are follow-up questions, the field will switch back to Siri AI for the next query. So if you want to use ChatGPT again, you'll need to manually choose it next time around.<br/>
<br/>
Another way to query ChatGPT directly is to start your spoken Siri request with "ask ChatGPT." The same phrasing works if you type it into the Search or Ask field.<br/>
<br/>
